Homepage: https://github.com/liamnewmarch/jellyfin-wake-hdd-service

Package: jellyfin-wake-hdd
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, curl, jq, systemd
Description: This package installs a systemd service which polls Jellyfin.
 When a client connects, it wakes hard disks so they’re ready for playback.
 .
 Enclosures with multiple drives that spin up in series can introduce a
 noticeable delay (several seconds) the first time Jellyfin reads from
 disk after an idle period, because the whole enclosure has to wake up
 before playback can start.
 .
 Configuration (Jellyfin URL, API key, and the paths to touch) lives in
 /etc/jellyfin-wake-hdd.conf.
